    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Find $Hn$ if\n$H=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$n=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $Hn=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Hn=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-10)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 1 \\\\ \u2217\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-43 \\\\ \u2217\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Hn=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-43 \\\\ 5\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-43 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$Hn=\\begin{bmatrix}-43 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}.$",
